                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "BUYER BEWARE - the game currently for sale is NOT THE SAME GAME that all the positive reviews refer to. \n\nI bought this game on 6-AUG-2020 and immediately feel in love with it. It really felt like playing the game, as opposed to the bloated AAA franchises, which try to mimic the experience of watching it on TV. Zippy and loads of fun.\n\nThen, 6 days later on 12-AUG, they posted an \"update.\" This update - or theft, if we're calling it what it is - involved deleting my new game from my library, and replacing it with a totally different game. All of the features - teams, tournaments, high-res graphics - all gone. It's been replaced by something that looks like it was written on a Commodore 64. What a joke. All I can figure is that they had some kind of copyright problem and got shut down, and needed to throw something together in its place, so they spent 24 hours throwing together some 8-bit code and some 4-bit graphics so that they could continue to collect our money despite stealing our game back. Think early Android quality here. \n\nI have requested a refund and strongly encourage other players to do the same. It may get denied but if enough people do it then maybe Valve will notice the scam these guys pulled.\n\n",
